WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.062
Let’s walk through Dashboard.

00:00:02.062 --> 00:00:04.675
Use the dashboard to detect drift, not to resolve

00:00:04.675 --> 00:00:05.325
it.

00:00:05.325 --> 00:00:08.625
Compare counts and recent activity with the selected session,

00:00:08.625 --> 00:00:11.675
then open the owning participant, RFI, session,

00:00:11.675 --> 00:00:14.350
or export surface before taking action.

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:17.825
On this slide, read active sessions, participant counts

00:00:17.825 --> 00:00:21.175
, pending RFIs, and recent activity at a glance

00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:21.337
.

00:00:21.337 --> 00:00:24.875
In practice, use the dashboard to detect operational drift

00:00:24.875 --> 00:00:27.988
, then open the owning surface before taking action.

00:00:28.485 --> 00:00:31.260
When you are ready, use Open Dashboard to move

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.735
to the live surface.

00:00:32.735 --> 00:00:35.435
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:35.585
.
